# docs/coverage-floors — per-module line-coverage floors (WI-279).
#
# Read by project-trajectory/scripts/check_coverage.py (wired as docs/stack.ini
# [step:module-coverage]). Each non-comment line is
#   <repo-relative module path>  <min line-coverage percent>
# `#` comments (whole-line or trailing) and blank lines are ignored, so each
# floor can carry a why-note (the declared-list idiom this kit uses everywhere:
# docs/orphans-allow, docs/declared-absences).
#
# WHY (repo-review 2026-07-22 M-4): the global [coverage] threshold (85) is ONE
# aggregate number, so heavily-tested generators subsidize thin coverage in the
# security/process boundaries below — the ~91% headline overstates confidence
# there. These per-module minimums are a REGRESSION SENSOR for exactly those
# modules; the global --cov-fail-under stays the backstop, not the only measure.
# Floors sit a few points below the honest measured baseline (jitter +
# cross-platform headroom — CI enforces on Linux/Windows/macOS, and the number is
# measured on one; the same stance as the global floor's ~6-point margin), so a
# real regression trips the gate while normal variation does not.
#
# MEASURED 2026-07-23 on the pinned toolchain (requirements-dev.txt), full tier:
#   agent_session.py 81.0%   subagent_gate.py 39.7%   plan_runner.py 79.6%
# RAISE a floor only alongside the focused behavioral tests that earn it, in the
# same commit — never a drive-by bump (the ratchet-only-tightens discipline the
# complexity/size ratchets already keep).

# The Windows batch-shim command-injection boundary (repo-review H-1) — a
# security control (still ~81% even after the H-1 regressions). EXTRA headroom
# here: this module has platform-divergent RUNTIME branches (os.name == "nt"
# PATHEXT/shim resolution covered only on Windows; the POSIX branches only on
# Linux/macOS), so its per-file percent legitimately shifts across the CI matrix
# in a way the branch-free modules below do not — the floor sits well under the
# Windows baseline so a real regression trips it without false-redding Linux/mac.
project-trajectory/scripts/agent_session.py   72

# The subagent policy gate — itself a safety control, and the weakest module the
# review named (~40%). This floor stops further erosion until a focused test
# campaign earns a higher one.
project-trajectory/scripts/subagent_gate.py   34

# The dual-plan planning adapter — a process-launch / planning boundary, ~80%.
project-trajectory/scripts/plan_runner.py   75
